# AoTv4 custom overlay: .devcontainer/custom/ holds the project's own source (custom Lua
# modules, global_player.lua edits, eq-core-dll source) which the Makefile applies onto the
# bootstrapped clones. Track it -- including the dll .vcxproj that the global *.vcxproj rule
# above would otherwise hide.
!.devcontainer/custom/**/*.vcxproj

# Large DB recovery dumps -- local backups only, never committed (see POST_REBUILD_RECOVERY.md)
/Deez.sql
/aotv4_current.sql
# Auto-generated migration pre-backup dumps (mysqldump, see CLAUDE.md §15) -- dated, 100s of MB, never commit
/peq_aotv4_*.sql
/peq_*_backup*.sql
client_dist/BaseData.txt
client_dist/dbstr_us.txt
client_dist/SkillCaps.txt
client_dist/spells_us.txt
aotv4_custom_spells.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- client UI XML (EQUI_*.xml)
# Stock and reference client UI files, wherever they land: the copies dropped at the repo root as
# SIDL references (EQUI_Animations, EQUI_Templates, EQUI_BazaarWnd, ...), a whole "default" uifiles
# folder copied in from the client, and anything under utils/. None of it is ours; every file is
# recoverable from any RoF2 install, and together they are thousands of lines of churn.
EQUI_*.xml
/default/
utils/EQUI_*.xml

# ⚠️ OUR OWN WINDOWS ARE NOT IGNORED, and must not be. The files below are hand-authored SOURCE and
# the repo is their only copy -- the dll looks each one up by screen name at runtime, so losing one
# means that window silently never appears again with no error anywhere. The blanket rule above
# would otherwise swallow them, because a pattern with no slash matches at ANY depth.
!aotv4_client_install/uifiles_default/EQUI_*.xml

# ...except the picker, which is GENERATED by aotv4_client_install/gen_choice_xml.pl from
# spell_icons.lua + skill_pool.lua. ~8600 lines that change wholesale on every pool regen; rerun the
# generator rather than diffing it.
aotv4_client_install/uifiles_default/EQUI_AoTSpellChoiceWnd.xml
